# JVM options for the sbt server of THIS checkout (sbt's readConfigFile skips #-comments).
#
# Read this before changing a number: the constraint here is not one server, it is thirteen.
# Parallel agents keep one resident sbt server per worktree, and on 2026-07-20 nineteen build JVMs
# held ~79 GB on a 36 GB host and the kernel watchdog force-rebooted the machine. Per-process caps
# were all fine. The sum was not.

-Xmx4G
-XX:+UseG1GC

# ── give idle memory BACK to the host (measured 2026-07-28, scripts/build-ram-idle-ab) ──────────
# An sbt server holds its peak heap forever once it goes idle, because G1 only returns memory to the
# OS at a full GC and an idle server never has one. JEP 346 periodic GC plus aggressive heap-free
# ratios turns that dead weight back into host RAM.
#
#   arm                       idle RSS    committed heap
#   baseline (no flags)        2698 MB         2108 MB     <- flat for 180 s, never returns a byte
#   periodic GC @15 s          1578 MB         1160 MB     <- drops at T+30 s
#   periodic GC @60 s          1553 MB         1158 MB     <- drops at T+120 s, SAME floor
#
# -1145 MB per idle server, -42 %. Across 13 live worktrees that is ~15 GB of a 36 GB host handed
# back. Both intervals reach the identical floor, so 60 s is chosen over 15 s: it costs 4x fewer
# idle full GCs for the same reclaim. Reproduce either arm with:
#   scripts/build-ram-idle-ab baseline
#   scripts/build-ram-idle-ab shrink "<flags>"
#
# `-XX:-G1PeriodicGCInvokesConcurrent` is the load-bearing one and is easy to drop by accident:
# with the default (+) G1 runs a CONCURRENT cycle, which collects but does NOT resize the heap, so
# the RSS never falls and the whole change measures as a no-op. The full GC is what shrinks.
# `G1PeriodicGCSystemLoadThreshold=0` disables the load gate; periodic GC still only fires when no
# GC happened during the interval, so an actively compiling server never pays for it.
-XX:MinHeapFreeRatio=10
-XX:MaxHeapFreeRatio=30
-XX:G1PeriodicGCInterval=60000
-XX:G1PeriodicGCSystemLoadThreshold=0
-XX:-G1PeriodicGCInvokesConcurrent
